    "created_at": "2024-01-22T18:36:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-22T18:36:34Z",
    "body": "Sorry, that should read \"true\". On the first byte, written is 0, destination's byte length the original size of the array, and the number of bytes in result is 1 between and 4 (I assume; anyway it's some finite number). So as long as the TA originally had at least 4 bytes, that check passes and we don't break.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
